==========================================================================
1. REACHABILITY vs STATIC FEEDER LIST, under reconfiguration
==========================================================================
  trials with reconfiguration: 400
  static MISSES a real violation :  327/400 =  81.8%   Wilson95 [77.7, 85.2]
  static FALSELY flags a legal one:    0/400 =   0.0%   Wilson95 [0.0, 1.0]
  agrees with reachability        :   73/400 =  18.2%
  A precomputed 'which DERs are on this feeder' list goes stale the
  moment a switch moves; the reachability query does not.

==========================================================================
2. k-ANONYMITY AS phi_Sigma  (k = 5)
==========================================================================
  detection of disclosing aggregates : 211/211 = 100.0%
  false positives on legal aggregates: 0/189 =   0.0%
  Unlike the lexical cue matcher the mission instantiation used, this
  is a computable property: exact by construction, not a heuristic.

==========================================================================
3. EVIDENCE COMPLETENESS UNDER TELEMETRY LOSS
==========================================================================
    loss  real violations   naive misses            aware flags         of which Fp    clean    incon.         
    0.00              122              0     0.0%           122   100.0%         0       78         0     0.0%
    0.10              116             12    10.3%           116   100.0%         0       84        61    72.6%
    0.25              121             32    26.4%           121   100.0%         0       79        79   100.0%
    0.50              135             69    51.1%           135   100.0%         0       65        65   100.0%
  A monitor that sums only what reported cannot distinguish a small
  aggregate from a large one it half observed. Flagging the gap is the
  difference between 'no violation' and 'no evidence'.

