4. COMPOSITION NECESSITY (empirical, not definitional)
==========================================================================
  per-device-legal dispatches violating an aggregate limit,
  as a function of fleet nameplate:
      DER kW  fleet kW  penetration   violating          Wilson95
         140      1820          49%      0/500   0.0%   [0.0, 0.8]
         280      3640          98%    315/500  63.0%   [58.7, 67.1]
         420      5460         147%    453/500  90.6%   [87.7, 92.9]
         560      7280         196%    486/500  97.2%   [95.4, 98.3]
         700      9100         245%    497/500  99.4%   [98.3, 99.8]
  at the modelled 140 kW rating the aggregate constraint does not bind: 0/500
    (this is the rate a per-device control would pass unchallenged --
     an empirical quantity, not the definitional observation that a
     per-device check cannot see an aggregate)

  configuration             missed   false pos
  phi_S only               385/385       0/115 
